1
00:00:01,221 --> 00:00:06,568
Jens: Everybody sees you are successful 'cause you write with a Montblanc Meisterstück. ——【Jens】

2
00:00:06,568 --> 00:00:12,031
When you're holding it, it just feels a little bit heavier and more luxurious. ——

3
00:00:12,031 --> 00:00:19,648
Axel: To produce a Meisterstück, if we just make one, it would take around about four to five weeks. ——【Axel】

4
00:00:19,648 --> 00:00:21,344
Jens: The branding is spectacular. ——【Jens】

5
00:00:21,344 --> 00:00:23,910
You see the star, know exactly what it is.

6
00:00:23,910 --> 00:00:27,649
Alexa: Kings use it, presidents use it, celebrities use it. ——【Alexa】

7
00:00:27,649 --> 00:00:31,344
Oh sure Richard, you can use my Montblanc. ——

8
00:00:31,344 --> 00:00:38,661
Jens: It's about 800, 900 euros. So it was always a status symbol and was very expensive. ——【Jens】

9
00:00:38,661 --> 00:00:58,417
We really intend them to be companions of unique journeys, and by nature, that means that people tend to use the Meisterstück when those moments occur. ——

10
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:07,817
The Meisterstück was first launched in 1924 and Meisterstück is German and means masterpiece.&nbsp;

11
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:11,752
It's not so easy to pronounce if you are not a native speaker.

12
00:01:11,752 --> 00:01:25,676
And legend has it that the pen already existed, but in the drawers of our master craftsmen, and then clients came and asked for a special pen for the Sunday use, so the pen of the pens.

13
00:01:25,676 --> 00:01:30,397
And this is when they pulled that one out of the drawer.

14
00:01:30,397 --> 00:01:43,868
Fountain pens were always this prestige object, but the Meisterstück was always high top of quality and with a lifetime guarantee, so people were secure to use it and they're proud to show it.

15
00:01:43,868 --> 00:01:51,271
So Montblanc was never an innovation leader and they copied a lot of other companies, but they done it in the best way you can do it.&nbsp;

16
00:01:51,271 --> 00:01:56,498
Be the fast follower, invest in the right marketing on high quality level.

17
00:01:56,498 --> 00:02:01,412
My grandfather was one of the founder of Montblanc.

18
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,758
I was surrounded with pens and pencils.

19
00:02:03,758 --> 00:02:08,689
And we tested him too, breaking, sometimes, things, and writing, and filling with ink.

20
00:02:08,689 --> 00:02:21,772
My grandfather and my father, too, told me the employers, the workforce has to be well-educated 'cause they're responsible at the end for the quality.

21
00:02:21,772 --> 00:02:24,920
I am in charge of the gold nib department.

22
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:28,831
I started at Montblanc over 35 years.

23
00:02:28,831 --> 00:02:36,837
When you have a nib produced in gold material, you can give the pen from generation to generation.

24
00:02:36,837 --> 00:02:39,511
If you can do that, you have no problem with corrosion.

25
00:02:39,511 --> 00:02:44,992
For the grinding process, we have over six months training and it's not for everybody.

26
00:02:44,992 --> 00:02:49,113
I think 50% cannot achieve the training level.

27
00:02:49,113 --> 00:02:51,896
You need very good eyes.

28
00:02:51,896 --> 00:02:54,139
You need very good dexterities.

29
00:02:54,139 --> 00:02:56,789
Your hand moving have to be very good.

30
00:02:56,789 --> 00:03:00,060
Also, high concentration is very important.

31
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:05,020
The perfect nib has to be not too loud.

32
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:11,248
We test every nib and every nib unit in my department by hand.

33
00:03:11,248 --> 00:03:22,390
The embossing, the characteristic design for Montblanc is a Montblanc logo and the 4,810 meters, the highest mountain in Europe.&nbsp;

34
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:31,104
Penmaker: When we ask people if they know the brand and what they know about the brand, one of the very first things they will mention is our emblem.&nbsp;

35
00:03:31,104 --> 00:03:36,847
So the snow cap that adorns every of our writing instruments.

36
00:03:36,847 --> 00:03:42,973
And that is a key recognition element that people really love about the brand.

37
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:51,205
The story of the star is interesting 'cause it is this typical story that design follows function.

38
00:03:51,205 --> 00:04:01,162
Mr. Eberstein, member of the first founder, had a patent on the cover cap top for fountain pens, but it was not protectable in Germany.

39
00:04:01,162 --> 00:04:10,841
So they were looking for another idea and they decided to make a star on the cap top.

40
00:04:10,841 --> 00:04:24,400
This precious resin just gives you a fantastic, deep, shiny surface that we really using for our icon.

41
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,068
It's a timeless color.

42
00:04:27,068 --> 00:04:33,281
It's a bit like in fashion, the little black dress, you can bring it to any occasion, any moment.

43
00:04:33,281 --> 00:04:38,010
We check the quality with a special light.

44
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:49,586
We are looking at the pen and, of course, and if you move it like this, you will see the flame looks like a candlelight, and it goes from the cone up to the Montblanc logo.

45
00:04:49,586 --> 00:05:00,229
It is a piece that we reinvent every year, which we use as a canvas for storytelling and which also inspires the creation of other pieces.

46
00:05:00,229 --> 00:05:06,975
There are a lot of different reasons why people write with fountain pens.

47
00:05:06,975 --> 00:05:13,794
I'm practicing calligraphy, doing monoline italic with a Meisterstück 146.

48
00:05:13,794 --> 00:05:17,361
You know, in monoline italic, you want something that is quite uniform.

49
00:05:17,361 --> 00:05:22,540
The pen, you know, writes very smoothly and there's not much variation, so this is very ideal.

50
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:26,896
Favorite pens of my collection to tell a little story, have much more.

51
00:05:26,896 --> 00:05:29,648
Here are three pens I'm very fond of.

52
00:05:29,648 --> 00:05:32,494
There's only one piece in the world you can have.

53
00:05:32,494 --> 00:05:33,664
This is a prototype.

54
00:05:33,664 --> 00:05:37,478
Right now, I love to write with the .

55
00:05:37,478 --> 00:05:43,072
I love this one because it's made out of wood and it feels really nice in the hand.

56
00:05:43,072 --> 00:05:47,444
For my signature, I write with a double broad BB.

57
00:05:47,444 --> 00:05:52,778
I usually keep about five pens inked and one will always be a Montblanc pen.

58
00:05:52,778 --> 00:05:56,439
When the mood strikes, I always know that it's always gonna work properly.

59
00:05:56,439 --> 00:06:00,411
I inherited one from my husband.

60
00:06:00,411 --> 00:06:04,882
He used to work in finance and he was using it for quite a bit.

61
00:06:04,882 --> 00:06:10,271
I think that the price of the Montblanc pen for me personally, may not be worth it.

62
00:06:10,271 --> 00:06:19,082
I think that I'm very lucky that I got my pen secondhand, and I know people personally that have inherited from, you know, their father or grandfather.

63
00:06:19,082 --> 00:06:26,338
If you come at it from that type of angle, I think that, you know, it's probably worth the price 'cause it's made to last that long.

64
00:06:26,338 --> 00:06:28,838
If this brand Montblanc will not exist, I think the idea of buying fountain pen as a status symbol will not be in the mind of many, many people who can afford the status symbol like a Montblanc pen.

